that threaten already tight winter inventories strained by Middle East export disruptions.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:47.065
Analysts rating changes after a broad sector correction can flag rotation candidates

00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:51.925
when they arrive with an earnings beat, and simply Wall Street's read on applied materials is

00:01:51.925 --> 00:01:57.245
the worked example. The company reported a beat and strong guidance into last week's AI-related

00:01:57.245 --> 00:02:02.585
pullback. You see a semi-conductor name print a beat and raise guidance in the middle of an AI-led

00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:08.965
washout, an analyst reiterates on the same day. Do you buy the print or do you wait? Here's how I'd

00:02:08.965 --> 00:02:14.025
think about it. Screen for upgrades or reiterations on the earnings date using your broker's newsfeed,

00:02:14.025 --> 00:02:18.425
Then cross-check the daily chart so you know whether price is actually holding above the

00:02:18.425 --> 00:02:19.665
50-day moving average.

00:02:20.345 --> 00:02:24.525
Enter only after that upgrade coincides with price above the average and with the volume

00:02:24.525 --> 00:02:29.125
filter confirming participation, which is how you keep a headline from becoming an order

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:30.805
during a sector-wide drawdown.

00:02:31.265 --> 00:02:35.965
That pairing worked in prior rotation periods when volume confirmed within two sessions,

00:02:36.385 --> 00:02:40.705
and it failed when geopolitical headlines forced indiscriminate selling that overrode

00:02:40.705 --> 00:02:41.165
the signal.

00:02:41.805 --> 00:02:45.385
Investors can run it by pulling the earnings transcript and the same day

00:02:45.385 --> 00:02:49.925
analyst notes, then overlaying a simple moving average scan in any charting

00:02:49.925 --> 00:02:54.065
platform to time the entry. When the earnings catalyst aligns with that

00:02:54.065 --> 00:02:58.505
technical filter, follow through over the subsequent five sessions has historically

00:02:58.505 --> 00:03:02.885
been cleaner than unfiltered entries on the print alone. Remember the

00:03:02.885 --> 00:03:07.889
catalyst opens the door, only participation walks you through it. Applied

00:03:07.889 --> 00:03:14.169
materials ticker AMAT on the NASDAQ is the simulated weekly hold, and this is a simulated

00:03:14.169 --> 00:03:19.189
trade for learning purposes with no real money. The earning surprise entry layers that

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:23.589
beat and guidance catalyst onto a rotation check during a sector-wide correction that

00:03:23.589 --> 00:03:29.489
erased more than $5 trillion from the S&amp;P 500 last week, which is today's upgrade after

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:34.869
correction screen rather than a bet on tech concentration. That concentration has shown mixed

00:03:34.869 --> 00:03:39.889
results in recent trades. Price action after the beat still has to hold the 50-day moving

00:03:39.889 --> 00:03:44.549
average, and the volume filter still has to confirm, or the print is just a headline.

00:03:45.289 --> 00:03:50.609
The thesis is done if applied materials posts a daily close under that 50-day average on any

00:03:50.609 --> 00:03:55.989
of the next five sessions, which is the invalidation named before the simulated money is at risk,

00:03:56.429 --> 00:04:02.789
not a feeling about the tape. The stop sits 8% below entry, which caps the simulated loss at $80

00:04:02.789 --> 00:04:07.949
dollars on the $1,000 position if it is breached intraday, while the five-session window

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:08.749
stays active.

00:04:09.329 --> 00:04:15.149
The target is plus 3% to plus 7% over those five sessions if follow through holds and the

00:04:15.149 --> 00:04:16.529
broader market stabilizes.

00:04:17.129 --> 00:04:18.189
Confidence is medium.

00:04:18.789 --> 00:04:23.389
The earnings catalyst is confirmed and rotation signals are present, but broader market

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:26.589
volatility is the uncertainty that keeps this off a high rating.

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:31.289
It enters at the next session's open under the published rules and is judged against

00:04:31.289 --> 00:04:36.749
the NASDAQ over those same five sessions. Open your platform, pull up applied materials,

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:40.649
check whether Friday's closed finished above its 50-day moving average,

00:04:41.309 --> 00:04:45.429
note the exact distance and set a price alert at that average so you get pinged

00:04:45.429 --> 00:04:50.909
if invalidation is approached during the hold. Monday's open put the simulated Costco position,

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:59.349
ticker cost, on at $1,111.18. A valuation comparison against Walmart on margins stability

00:04:59.349 --> 00:05:08.129
and membership growth, and Friday's close on November 20th, 2026, took it off at $1,102.15

00:05:08.129 --> 00:05:17.909
after five sessions. The simulated $1,000 position lost $8.13, or 0.81%. The NASDAQ over

00:05:17.909 --> 00:05:25.369
that same Monday to Friday window fell 9%, so the hold produced plus 8.19% of alpha, even

00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:30.089
the line itself finished slightly red, and honestly that relative result feels pretty

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:30.429
good.

00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:34.229
Stated confidence was low, and that grade fit a mixed setup.

00:05:34.749 --> 00:05:39.949
The invalidation, Walmart's same store sales below consensus in its next quarterly release,

00:05:40.489 --> 00:05:45.889
never mattered, and the 8% stop was never reached even while the index posted a sharp decline.

00:05:46.609 --> 00:05:51.469
The stop did its job by staying out of the way, and the low confidence rating was the honest

00:05:51.469 --> 00:05:54.709
call on a comparison that was never a high-conviction catalyst.

00:05:55.389 --> 00:06:00.229
The hold also argued for applying the volume filter before the next earnings-driven rotation

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:03.869
entry, which is already sitting on today's applied materials ticket.

