00:09:30.698 --> 00:09:37.798
The full history since March 2026 covers 110 trades with a 52% win rate and accumulative loss

00:09:37.798 --> 00:09:45.358
of $802.70, which is context not the rules-based record that started on August 18, 2026,

00:09:45.938 --> 00:09:50.698
under fixed five session holds, next open entries, and stop or horizon exits.

00:09:50.698 --> 00:09:57.214
A trader holding leveraged AI positions in Taiwan watched margin calls multiply 200 fold

00:09:57.214 --> 00:10:02.294
last week as prices collapsed, and those forced exits amplified the down draft across

00:10:02.294 --> 00:10:03.274
the broader market.

00:10:03.914 --> 00:10:08.774
Rising margin calls forced sales regardless of anyone's fundamental view, which is less

00:10:08.774 --> 00:10:12.394
like a change of mind and more like a stadium emptying through one tunnel.

00:10:12.954 --> 00:10:15.394
People still in their seats are not wrong about the game.

00:10:15.814 --> 00:10:20.614
They are stuck in the crush, spreads widen, and price gaps away from fair value until

00:10:20.614 --> 00:10:21.874
the force selling is done.

00:10:22.814 --> 00:10:26.954
Professionals watch the ratio of margin debt to market cap and set alerts when it spikes

00:10:26.954 --> 00:10:28.274
beyond recent averages.

00:10:28.854 --> 00:10:33.374
Then wait until that liquidation wave peaks and volume begins to stabilize before they

00:10:33.374 --> 00:10:33.854
step in.

00:10:34.494 --> 00:10:38.654
The mistake is treating the resulting print as a permanent fundamental shift and selling

00:10:38.654 --> 00:10:43.414
into the worst bid, which locks in a loss that patients on the exchange's own margin

00:10:43.414 --> 00:10:44.774
debt reports would have avoided.

00:10:45.334 --> 00:10:50.474
In that Taiwan episode, one broker sent empathetic messages after handling an unusually

00:10:50.474 --> 00:10:55.354
high volume of calls, which is a useful tell that leverage is unwinding at an extreme.

00:10:56.074 --> 00:10:59.314
I have sold into a washout like that, and the fill was the lesson.

00:10:59.934 --> 00:11:03.714
The fundamental view was still intact, the exit ramp was just jammed.

00:11:04.174 --> 00:11:09.134
Track public exchange margin debt trends, rather than reacting to price alone, and wait

00:11:09.134 --> 00:11:13.954
for forced liquidation to subside before you add risk, because that crush repeats whenever

00:11:13.954 --> 00:11:16.314
concentrated leverage sits in a single theme.

